  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The Tsardom of Moscavia is a sprawling northern realm stretching across the forests and river valleys between the Ash Mountains to the west and the frozen shores of the Pale Sea to the north.",
      "since": null,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "Every living person within its borders was transformed into an owl-folk on the morning of 15 October in the year 998, an event known simply as the Turning.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "history",
      "text": "Before the Turning, Moscavia was a powerful human kingdom ruled by the Rurikovich dynasty, with a long history of warfare, trade, and cultural exchange along the northern routes.",
      "since": null,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "history",
      "text": "The Tsardom's capital is Velikigrad, a great city of stone and timber that has been thoroughly adapted for owl-folk habitation since 998.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "government",
      "text": "The Tsardom is governed by Tsar Dmitri Rurikovich III, who rules from Velikigrad with the aid of a council of twelve senior officials known as the Nocturnal Duma.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "government",
      "text": "The Nocturnal Duma conducts all official business between dusk and dawn, as the owl-folk are most alert during these hours; daytime is reserved for rest, commerce, and private affairs.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "law",
      "text": "Moscavian law has been revised extensively since the Turning to account for the physical and perceptual changes of the population, including new building codes, flight corridors over cities, and regulations on nocturnal hunting.",
      "since": 999,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "military",
      "text": "The Moscavian military, known as the Taloned Host, consists of aerial squadrons, ground infantry adapted with talon-gripping equipment, and a navy of modified vessels with high perch-decks for owl-folk officers.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The owl-folk of Moscavia have maintained their pre-Turning institutions — the Orthodox Church of the Northern Light, the merchant guilds, the academies of philosophy — though each has undergone significant transformation.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "No natural owl-folk were born before the Turning; every owl-folk citizen was once a human being, and they retain full memories of their human lives, which informs their culture, manners, and governance.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The cause of the Turning remains one of the great unsolved mysteries of Moscavian intellectual life, investigated by scholars in universities and monasteries across the realm.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "In the year 1000, Moscavia stands as a prosperous and stable realm, its transformation now a generation old, with a new culture that blends human memory with avian instinct.",
      "since": 1000,
      "held_by": null
    }
  ],
