  "tag": "institution, academy",
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The Academy of the Chiseled Moon is a training institution of the Order of the Talon-Scribe, located in the capital city of Velikoye.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "It serves as the primary training hall for the Quill of Teaching in Velikoye, preparing new scribes and advancing the studies of those already sworn into the Order.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "history",
      "text": "The Academy was established in Velikoye during the rebuilding efforts following the Turning of 998, replacing an earlier human scriptorium that had been destroyed in the hasty architectural conversion of the city.",
      "since": "999",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The building itself is a converted human guildhall on the fourth terrace of the city's eastern hill, its stone façade now fitted with wide flight-entrance archways, perch-ledges along every exterior wall, and reinforced rooftop bracing designed to bear the weight of dozens of roosting owl-folk.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "Inside, the main lecture hall is a vaulted chamber of grey stone, its walls lined with alcoves containing inscribed tablets — practice texts carved by generations of students since the Academy's founding.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The hall features twelve long desks arranged in concentric semicircles around a raised dais where the master scribe stands, each desk equipped with a sloping writing surface, a tray of iron styluses, and a block of pale limestone for rune practice.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "law",
      "text": "Admission to the Academy requires a letter of recommendation from a Talon-Scribe of the Quill of Memory or Quill of the Field, attesting to the candidate's literacy and aptitude for rune-inscription.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Students at the Chiseled Moon train for a minimum of two years, during which they learn the First Circle runes, the foundational scripts of the Tsardom, and advance to the more complex Frostward Runes used in military and diplomatic inscription work.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Academy's curriculum also includes history, calligraphy, and the philosophical tenets of the Order, including the significance of the Oath of the Unbroken Line and the belief that runes are a living language of the land itself.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The head of the Academy holds the title of Master of the Chiseled Moon, appointed by the Ataman of the Quill in consultation with the Quill of Teaching's senior scribes.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "By the year 1000, the Academy has graduated over three hundred Talon-Scribes, many of whom have gone on to distinguished careers in all three Quills of the Order.",
      "since": "1000",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Academy's motto, carved above its main entrance in deep ochre paint against grey stone, reads: 'What is written endures' — the same phrase that adorns the entrance to the Ataman's Citadel in Khorov.",
      "held_by": null
    }
  ],
