  "name": "Frostwing Host",
  "aka": [
    {
      "name": "The Wing",
      "tag": "common",
      "everyday": true
    }
  ],
  "tag": "military",
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Frostwing Host is the standing army of the Tsardom of Moscavia, fielded to defend the realm's borders and enforce its sovereignty across the northern reaches.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "It is organized into multiple specialized regiments, each tailored to the unique demands of Moscavia's terrain, from frozen glacier edges to dense boreal forests.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Every soldier of the Frostwing Host was once a human citizen of Moscavia who underwent the Turning of 998, and the army's doctrine reflects the blend of human tactical tradition and avian perceptual abilities inherited from that transformation.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Host maintains permanent garrisons along the Ash Mountains in the west, the northern glacier edge bordering the Pale Sea, and at key river crossing points along the Khorol and Kolyma systems.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Aerial squadrons constitute the Host's primary strike force, utilizing the natural flight capabilities of the owl-folk to conduct reconnaissance, rapid deployment, and high-altitude bombardment using modified siege equipment.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Ground infantry regiments are equipped with talon-gripping harnesses and reinforced armor plating designed to allow owl-folk soldiers to scale cliffs, ice faces, and vertical structures with devastating speed.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Host's navy operates a fleet of high-deck vessels along the Khorol and Kolyma rivers as well as the northern coast of the Pale Sea, with elevated command platforms built into the rigging for owl-folk officers to survey the battlefield.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Training for the Frostwing Host takes place at military academies in Velikoye and at regional garrison forts, where recruits are drilled in both the ancient human arts of warfare and the instinct-driven combat techniques unique to owl-folk physiology.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Host answers ultimately to Tsar Dmitri Rurikovich III and the Nocturnal Duma, with operational command delegated to a High Marshal appointed by the Tsar.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Elite regiments within the Host, such as the Frosted Wing and the White Talon, receive specialized training for arctic warfare and heavy assault respectively, and are considered the finest fighting forces in the known north.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Host's standard insignia is a silver owl clutching a sword against a field of deep blue, representing the union of the realm's avian nature with its martial heritage.",
      "held_by": null
    }
  ],
