  "tag": "institution",
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Order of the Talon-Scribe is the sovereign institution tasked with the preservation, interpretation, and teaching of the Tsardom's runic traditions."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Founded in the year 312, the Order emerged from the royal decree of Tsar Aleksandr I, who recognized that the scattered and orally transmitted rune-knowledge of the realm's many peoples needed centralized governance to prevent its fragmentation."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Order's seat is the Citadel of Inked Stone, a fortified monastery complex in the city of Velikhor, the Tsardom's cultural heart."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Order is led by the Grand Scribe, a figure appointed for life by the reigning Tsar from among the Order's most accomplished and senior members."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Beneath the Grand Scribe, the Order is divided into five ranks: Aspirant, Novice, Scribe, Senior Scribe, and Arch-Scribe."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Aspirants are candidates who have demonstrated aptitude in the rune arts but have not yet taken the Oath of the Talon. Novices are those who have taken the Oath and begun formal study. Scribes are those who have completed their education and serve in chapters across the Tsardom. Senior Scribes oversee regional chapters, and Arch-Scribes sit on the Council of the Talon, advising the Grand Scribe."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Order maintains seven chapters across the Tsardom, each situated in a major city or fortress town: Velikhor, Khorvash, Dunmor, Starye Kameni, the Fortress of Ashenveil, the riverside town of Oryol, and the mountain citadel of Krepky."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Every member of the Order takes the Oath of the Talon upon elevation to the rank of Novice, swearing to uphold the integrity of the rune-knowledge, to never use the runes for personal gain or harm, and to submit all discoveries to the Order's archives."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Order's archives, known as the Vast Ledger, are housed in the deepest vaults of the Citadel of Inked Stone and are considered among the most comprehensive repositories of knowledge in the known world."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Order's members are identifiable by the black talon-shaped amulet they wear at the breast, etched with the rune of binding oath, which is never removed in life or in death."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Order has historically served as the Tsardom's official body for inscribing state documents, legal codes, treaties, and royal decrees, giving its work a direct bearing on governance and law."
    },
    {
      "category": "belief",
      "text": "The Order teaches that the runes are not merely symbols but living expressions of the fundamental forces that shape the world, and that their proper understanding requires both intellectual study and moral discipline."
    }
  ],
