  "tag": "military institution",
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The White Talon is the heavy regiment of the Frostwing Host, the standing army of the Kingdom of Valdenmere."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "It was founded in the year 743 by King Aldric II to serve as the kingdom's elite strike force in mountainous and frozen terrain."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Recruits must survive a six-month trial known as the Frosting, held at the fortress of Karrath Hold in the Greypeak Mountains, to earn the right to wear the regiment's insignia."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The insignia of the White Talon is a talon claw wrought in white iron, worn pinned to the left breast of the surcoat."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Soldiers of the White Talon are issued layered plate-and-mail armor forged at the royal armories of Ironhaven, designed to withstand temperatures as low as minus thirty degrees."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The regiment is currently commanded by General Maren Ashvale, a woman of forty-two winters who earned her rank after the Battle of Thornpass in 987."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The White Talon numbers roughly one thousand five hundred soldiers at full muster, organized into seven companies named after predators of the northern wilderness: Wolf, Lynx, Hawk, Wraith, Ram, Vulture, and Bear."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Each soldier swears the Oath of the White Talon upon completion of the Frosting, pledging to stand firm even when all others fall, to never abandon a comrade alive on the field, and to die rather than surrender their post."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The regiment's standard-bearer carries a banner of deep blue cloth bearing the white talon emblem, and it is said that the banner has been torn and re-stitched forty-seven times across the regiment's history."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The White Talon maintains its headquarters and primary barracks at Karrath Hold, a stone fortress built into the mountainside at an elevation of nearly eight thousand feet."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Soldiers of the White Talon are permitted to grow beards and braid their hair with white cord, distinguishing them from the shaved heads of common soldiers in the Frostwing Host."
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The regiment is widely regarded as the most disciplined and deadly fighting force in the northern reaches of the continent, feared by enemies and revered by the people of Valdenmere."
    }
  ],
